      <notesStmt>
        <note type="scope" xml:lang="eng">
          <p>This file carries only the first 50 verses of the Kāñcippurāṇam
          (the complete பாயிரம், verses 1&#8211;27, plus an opening excerpt of
          திருநாட்டுப்படலம், verses 28&#8211;50 of that chapter's 28&#8211;172).
          It is a working excerpt for demonstrating the encoding pipeline at a
          realistic scale, not a complete critical edition of the text. Verse
          numbering and chapter (படலம்) divisions follow the source etext
          exactly. Prosody/meter labels given in the source between verse
          numbers (e.g. கலிநிலைத் துறை, வேறு) are encoded as
          <mentioned>note[@type="meter"]</mentioned> rather than as verse
          content. Only one witness is available for this excerpt, so no
          apparatus variants (<mentioned>app</mentioned>/<mentioned>lem</mentioned>/<mentioned>rdg</mentioned>)
          are encoded here; see
          <ref target="../../docs/encoding-guidelines.md">encoding guidelines</ref>
          for how to add a second witness later. Named-entity tagging
          (<mentioned>placeName</mentioned>/<mentioned>persName</mentioned>) has
          not been applied to this excerpt, which is normal and expected per the
          guidelines. The <mentioned>@corresp</mentioned> alignment to the
          Sanskrit companion file used by the earlier synthetic sample has been
          removed: this real Tamil excerpt is not a verified translation or
          parallel recension of that (still-synthetic) Sanskrit sample, and a
          verse-level correspondence has not been established.</p>
        </note>
